<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uprising of Asen and Peter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1185–1187</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uprising of Asen and Peter was the revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlachs">Vlachs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a> against Byzantine rule, begun in 1185 by the brothers Theodore-Peter and Ivan Asen. Sparked by heavy taxation, it defeated several Byzantine expeditions and by 1187 had established the Second Bulgarian Empire, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliko-tarnovo">Tarnovo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uprising-of-asen-and-peter.jpg" alt="Uprising of Asen and Peter" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Bulgarian_Empire_(1185-1196).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
